.\" -*- groff -*-
.\"
.TH XLIO 8 "#BUILD_DATE#" libxlio "XLIO(#PRJ_LIBRARY_MAJOR#.#PRJ_LIBRARY_MINOR#.#PRJ_LIBRARY_REVISION#) User's Manual"
.SH NAME
xlio_stats \- Accelerated IO SW library (XLIO) statistic utility.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xlio_stats
[\-p \fIpid\fP] [\-k \fIdirectory\fP] [\-v \fIview\fP] [\-d \fIdetails\fP] [\-i \fIinterval\fP]
[\-n \fIapplication\fP] [\-f] [\-F] [\-c \fIcycles\fP] [\-l \fIlevel\fP] [\-z]

.SH DESCRIPTION
xlio_stats is program that reports information about sockets and internal related objects for xlio (7).
xlio_stats can be configured using command-line options

The options are as follows:
.sp
\fB\-p,\-\-pid\fP \fIid\fP
Show XLIO statistics for process with pid.
.TP
\fB\-k,\-\-directory\fP=\fIdirectory\fP
Set shared memory directory path.
.TP
\fB\-n,\-\-name\fP=\fIapplication\fP
Show XLIO statistics for application.
.TP
\fB\-f,\-\-find_pid\fP
Find and show statistics for XLIO instance running.
.TP
\fB\-F,\-\-forbid_clean\fP
By setting this flag inactive shared objects would not be removed.
.TP
\fB\-i,\-\-interval\fP=\fIinterval\fP
Print report every interval seconds.
.TP
\fB\-c,\-\-cycles\fP=\fIcycles\fP
Do report print cycles and exit, use 0 value for infinite.
.TP
\fB\-v,\-\-view\fP=\fI[1|2|3|4|5]\fP
Set view type: 1\- basic info, 2\- extra info, 3\- full info, 4\- mc groups, 5\- similar to 'netstat \-tunaep'.
.TP
\fB\-d,\-\-details\fP=\fI[1|2]\fP
Set details mode:1\- to see totals, 2\- to see deltas.
.TP
\fB\-z,\-\-zero\fP
Zero counters.
.TP
\fB\-l,\-\-log_level\fP=\fIlevel\fP
Set XLIO log level (one of: none, panic, error, warn, info, details, debug, fine, finer, all).
.TP
\fB\-S,\-\-fd_dump\fP=\fIfd [level]\fP
Dump statistics for fd number using log level. Use 0 value for all open fds.
.TP
\fB\-D,\-\-details_level\fP=\fIlevel\fP
Set XLIO log details level.
.TP
\fB\-s,\-\-sockets\fP=\fI[list|range]\fP
Log only sockets that match list or range, format: 4-16 or 1,9 (or combination).
.TP
\fB\-V,\-\-version\fP
Print version.
.TP

.SH RX LAYOUT CAPTURE
Use --rx-layout with -p to request bounded TCP receive-layout batches:
.PP
.nf
xlio_stats -p PID --rx-layout --rx-samples 256 -i 1 -c 10
.fi
.PP
--rx-samples selects 1 to 256 records per ring (default 256).
The interval must be at least one second. -c counts display updates, including
updates without samples; zero means unlimited updates. Capture cannot be combined
with view, detail, socket-filter, CSV, logging, counter-reset or dump options.
.PP
The target must use a library with the capture extension. Capture requires write
access to its statistics file. Only one capture reader can hold the file lock;
ordinary statistics readers can run concurrently without requesting captures.
.PP
Before any eligible samples arrive, the view prints "No traffic". A partial batch
prints "Collecting samples (n/N)" and persists across updates. Each request inspects
at most four times the requested number of successful, non-filler completions;
unsupported or malformed packets count as excluded. That inspection limit, or a
ring closing, can publish a short or empty batch. CQ errors and STRQ fillers are
not inspected and are not included in the excluded count.
.PP
Tables show common layouts ordered by sample count. Prefix is the space before
Ethernet; Hdr is L2 + IP + TCP bytes, excluding Prefix. Frame is the normalized
completion length, excluding the prefix but possibly including Ethernet padding.
Payload is derived from IP and TCP lengths and excludes Ethernet padding.
Offset is the payload position relative to the receive slot. A%64 is the actual
payload address modulo 64; L%64 is payload length modulo 64. Data alignment
percentages exclude control-only packets. LRO identifies the aggregate segment
count, normalized to one for a non-aggregated completion.
.PP
These are RX completion samples, taken before software GRO. They are not PCIe
transaction sizes or on-wire sizes including FCS/preamble. LRO aggregates do not
reveal every constituent segment's length or alignment. Percentages describe each
ring's short sampled burst, not its traffic over the entire display interval.
.PP
Capture adds one state check per eligible completion while inactive. Only an
outstanding request enables diagnostic parsing and record writes. If the reader
exits, the outstanding bounded batch can finish; a later reader adopts it.
There are 16 capture slots per process. Retired unread slots remain pinned until
a reader consumes them. Rings denied a slot continue normal networking but remain
unsampled for their lifetime; the view reports the registration failure count.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xlio (7)

